/-!
# Structurality from `Equation2571` through a two-guard companion

Generated by `defwork/itautcell2.py`.  `Equation2571` is `x = (y ◇ ((z ◇ x) ◇ y)) ◇ x`.  Its guarded obligation
-- a bijection of a finite model commuting with `x □ y = if (M.op a b) = a then b else if (M.op a b) = b then a else (M.op a b)` is an automorphism of `◇` --
is `GuardAut2_pxy_x_pxy_y_y_x_pxy_Equation2571`, proved elsewhere.  That obligation names no target, so every
law the companion satisfies is another cell for free, and there
are 2 of them below.
